{
  "kanji": "館",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 館\ntitle: hall; large building\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 16\nradical: 食\nradicalNumber: 184\nonyomi: [カン]\nkunyomi: [やかた, たて]\ndistractors: [飯, 飲, 銀]\n---\n\n# 館 — hall; large building\n\n**Strokes:** 16 · **Key (radical):** 食 (no. 184) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n館 often names a **building with a particular purpose**, such as a library, cinema, or inn.\nIt is not a word you can freely add to any noun to name a building.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine the roofed right-hand 官 as a large hall with stacked rooms,\nand the [食](食.md)-shaped left side as a meal served inside. This is a visual aid, not historical evidence.\n\n## Readings\n\nThis table is selective; metadata also retains たて.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| カン | on | [図書館](../words/図書館.md) としょかん (library); 映画館 えいがかん (cinema) |\n| やかた | kun | 館 やかた (mansion; manor, literary) |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [図書館](../words/図書館.md) としょかん — library\n- 映画館 えいがかん — cinema; movie theater\n- 旅館 りょかん — traditional Japanese inn\n\n## Notes\n\n館（やかた）is not the everyday word for any ordinary building. For beginner vocabulary, prioritize\nthe カン compounds above.\n\n[院](院.md) also appears in institution names, but the two endings are not interchangeable.\n[飯](飯.md) and [飲](飲.md) have similar left sides; recognize 官 on the right to identify 館.\n",
